wcristalle@hotmail.com writes:
>
> Just out of curiosity, can you behead/bisect yourself by throwing
> Vorpal or the Tsurugi (sp?) up in the air?

No, looking at the source, the special beheading/bisection attacks are
skipped in this case, *except* if you're polymorphed into a Jabberwock
and throw Vorpal Blade upwards.  In this case, it'll behead you and
you'll turn back into your original form (or die if you have
unchanging).

Other artifacts *will* generally do their special damage:  Magicbane
can stun you, Fire Brand can burn you, and so on.

> Or do you just do a lot of damage?

Well, if unenchanted, Vorpal Blade does 1+d8, and the Tsurugi does
d8+d16 (ouch!), I believe.  However, if you're wearing a metallic
helmet, it'll protect you, and you'll only get one hit point of damage
(plus any increase damage bonus from a ring you're wearing).

By the way, if you're killed this way by a "normal" object, your cause
of death is "killed by a falling object".  However, if you throw a
cockatrice corpse up in the air without a helmet and stone yourself,
then you'll be "petrified by elementary physics".

